WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:03.110
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:08.510
- My name is Kelly McLemore, co-organizer

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.963
of Corgi Beach Day.

00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:12.358
Our dog, Mr. Pickles, was on Facebook

00:00:12.358 --> 00:00:15.163
back in October 2012, and we decided that

00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:17.404
we wanted to meet some
Facebook dogs in person

00:00:17.404 --> 00:00:18.810
and their owners.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.004
So the first one that we had,

00:00:20.004 --> 00:00:21.817
we had about 12 Corgis here

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:23.324
and then we decided to do another one

00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:25.427
and 75 Corgis showed up,

00:00:25.427 --> 00:00:28.467
then it was 250, 300, 400,

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.486
and today it's probably
close to 600 maybe.

00:00:31.486 --> 00:00:34.635
(upbeat music)

00:00:42.551 --> 00:00:44.047
- I didn't think it would grow this big,

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:46.228
but I'm definitely
thinking it's going to get

00:00:46.228 --> 00:00:47.283
even bigger than this.

00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.063
- This is her first time at the beach.

00:00:49.063 --> 00:00:50.607
She's not digging the water,

00:00:50.607 --> 00:00:52.682
but she loves the sand.

00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:54.427
- I met, Winston, the white Corgi

00:00:54.427 --> 00:00:56.760
who I do follow and that
was pretty exciting.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.489
He keeps coming over to drink our water.

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:00.660
My name is Tina and I'm
the proud mom of Winston

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.321
the white Corgi right here.

00:01:02.321 --> 00:01:04.189
There's a lot of people
who love him obviously,

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:05.744
but all he wants to do is play fetch.

00:01:05.744 --> 00:01:07.265
We're just trying to have a blast

00:01:07.265 --> 00:01:08.903
and make sure we say hi to everyone

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.664
and it's fun.

00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:12.189
- It's kind of overwhelming for him.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:14.998
He made me carry him
from the car a mile away.

00:01:14.998 --> 00:01:15.854
- She's a puppy.

00:01:15.854 --> 00:01:16.925
She's about four months old.

00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:18.086
We've been here for about three hours

00:01:18.086 --> 00:01:19.758
and she was done after an hour.

00:01:19.758 --> 00:01:20.826
- These are my two Corgis.

00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:23.659
They're wearing left shark
and right shark costumes.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:27.200
- We are one of the original
12 Corgis that were here

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.264
in October 2012.

00:01:29.427 --> 00:01:32.865
Today they are dressed
as Mexican (mumbling).

00:01:32.865 --> 00:01:33.762
- This is our dog.

00:01:33.762 --> 00:01:34.723
- Carrot.

00:01:34.723 --> 00:01:36.770
He's just been a very athletic dog.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:40.425
- Eventually he learned to
bounce the ball with his nose.

00:01:40.425 --> 00:01:43.535
(crowd cheering)

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:45.380
- [Voiceover] What does the
world love about Corgis so much?

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.483
- They're great companions.

00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:47.527
They're good looking dogs.

00:01:47.527 --> 00:01:49.466
- They're fun, they're intelligent,

00:01:49.466 --> 00:01:50.500
they're loving.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.719
She cuddles.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:53.425
She'll talk to you.

00:01:53.425 --> 00:01:55.816
- They have the stumpy
legs and they run around

00:01:55.816 --> 00:01:58.108
and fall over things easily
because they're so small

00:01:58.108 --> 00:01:59.787
and their tongue is always hanging out,

00:01:59.787 --> 00:02:02.202
so they're kind of entertaining
just to watch on their own.

00:02:02.202 --> 00:02:03.853
- When they jump in the air

00:02:03.853 --> 00:02:06.218
the bottom part just like
follows up with them, you know?

00:02:06.218 --> 00:02:09.444
It's just like a huge wave, you know?

00:02:09.444 --> 00:02:11.245
- The only thing about them is they shed

00:02:11.245 --> 00:02:13.405
and I've had probably 10
different breeds of dogs

00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:14.984
and I keep coming back to the Corgi.

00:02:14.984 --> 00:02:17.526
- I'm Susan from Queen's
Best Stumpy Dog Rescue.

00:02:17.526 --> 00:02:19.396
We're a rescue that specializes in Corgis

00:02:19.396 --> 00:02:20.543
and Corgi mixes.

00:02:20.543 --> 00:02:23.561
There are plenty of pure
bred Corgis that need homes.

00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:25.581
To this date, we've placed
about 30 dogs in homes.

00:02:25.581 --> 00:02:28.376
(upbeat music)

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.642
- We love Buzz Feed, bye.

